Subject: [PATCH] build: package tracedump and tracenode in vpp-plugin-core
Track: V18 (docs/vpp-code-track.md), D-077 — build configuration only, no C code
Status: optional — applied only by `build.sh --trace-plugins core`; the default build keeps upstream packaging
Upstream: not submitted (upstream intentionally ships them in vpp-plugin-devtools)

Upstream 26.06 builds tracedump/tracenode but ships them in vpp-plugin-devtools,
together with unittest/perfmon/oddbuf/bufmon/dispatch_trace/tracepath, which the
appliance does not install. Moving the two CMake components to vpp-plugin-core
makes their binary APIs (tracedump.api, graph.api, tracenode.api) available on a
product install without shipping the devtools package.

--- a/src/plugins/tracedump/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/plugins/tracedump/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -28,5 +28,5 @@
   tracedump_test.c
 
   COMPONENT
-  vpp-plugin-devtools
+  vpp-plugin-core
 )
--- a/src/plugins/tracenode/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/plugins/tracenode/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -33,5 +33,5 @@
   test.c
 
   COMPONENT
-  vpp-plugin-devtools
+  vpp-plugin-core
 )
